ential. With nearly $290K raised and over 22 million $TAP tokens already grabbed in the Digitap presale, investors are after something bigger than short-term price swings. At just $0.0125 in Round 1, $TAP is priced like a penny stock with blue-chip ambitions. The next round jumps to $0.0159. And this will hand over early buyers a stunning 27% profit before the year is even out. And this could mean $TAP is the best crypto to buy now. While ADA needs to fight to get back above resistance, Digitap is already a hot topic before its listing. It brings utility today and growth tomorrow. That’s why investors are filling their wallets with Digitap ($TAP) before its potential 50x price jump post-launch. Alt Coins to Watch: Cardano’s Struggles vs Digitap’s Rise Momentum still leans bullish, at least for now. Buyers haven’t thrown in the towel, and a solid bounce could unlock a path back to $0.92 or even $0.96, assuming volume shows up. That said, the outlook isn’t without cracks. Some dormant wallets are back in the game, larger holders appear to be cashing out, and on-chain data hints at weakening sentiment. ADA could end up stuck in its current range. ADA will be testing nerves while the market waits for a catalyst that may not arrive until later in Q4 2025. For now, if $0.84 crumbles, the ADA price slide could be quick toward $0.76 or lower. That would rattle sentiment and push investors to rethink ADA’s short-term prospects. On the other hand, Digitap remains on the higher ground. With no heavy baggage, a working presale, and a clear use case, $TAP gives investors the asymmetric upside Cardano can’t promise right now. In other words, at a time when ADA struggles for momentum, Digitap is grabbing headlines as the best crypto to buy now. Best Crypto to Buy Now: Cardano or Digitap? Cardano’s path in Q4 looks like a coin toss. Strong support zones are holding, but whale moves and dormant wallets keep adding pressure to one of the top 10 altcoins. That’s why analysts are split