yer 2 blockchain designed to cut fees, increase speed, and protect against bots. Unlike most meme coins that only thrive on culture, this one builds real infrastructure while keeping its fun identity. It has passed a Certik audit with a strong score, is already listed on CoinMarketCap, and is running a $777K giveaway and a Mega Giveaway with 15 ETH prizes for top presale buyers between stage 12 and stage 17. Why Little Pepe may overshadow XRP The difference between XRP and Little Pepe comes down to growth potential. For XRP to move from $3 to $10 is a 230% jump. For LILPEPE, even conservative projections suggest a potential 50x rise from its current presale price of $0.0022 if adoption and community growth take off after launch. The risk is obviously higher, but the upside is far larger. The numbers back this up. XRP’s market cap at the time of writing is over $160 billion which makes significant moves harder. LILPEPE, by contrast, is starting small, giving it room to expand if listings, marketing, and its Layer 2 ecosystem succeed. The fact that it peaked above PEPE, Dogecoin, and Shiba Inu in search volume between June and August shows that the project already has real traction among retail investors. Final thoughts XRP will always have its place in payments and the ETF narrative may keep it in the spotlight. But when it comes to raw growth potential, Little Pepe looks like the more exciting play today. With its presale price at $0.0022, Certik audit, CoinMarketCap listing, and community-focused giveaways, it is positioning itself as more than just another meme. Investors still have a chance to buy in before the presale closes and capture possible 36.36% gains before launch. For those looking at the bigger picture, the 50x potential from presale to future adoption may be the story that overshadows XRP’s $10 target. To learn more, check out the ongoing Little Pepe presale , join the community on Telegram , and follow the latest updates on Twitter . For more informa